Run order: build once -> Habitat -> robot model -> RViz -> runner (map) -> motion planner (path).
Wait for each step's "ready" line before starting the next one.

terminal 1  (build once - do NOT rebuild while the other terminals are running)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
rm -rf build install log
colcon build --packages-select robo_project vinebot_description
source install/setup.bash

terminal 2  (Habitat)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
python3 src/robo_project/habitat_bridge_vinebot_2.py
# ready when: "Robot spawned at x=-4.10 y=4.90" and "Habitat Bridge fully initialized"
# options:  --ros-args -p start_x:=-4.1 -p start_y:=4.9 -p start_yaw:=0.0
#           -p gpu_device_id:=-1    (no NVIDIA GPU / VM: software rendering)
#           -p show_window:=false   (no camera window)

terminal 3  (robot model)

cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch vinebot_description robot_launch.py

terminal 4  (RViz: map, robot, planned path, goal, current waypoint)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
rviz2 -d src/vinebot_description/config/display_vinebot.rviz

terminal 5  (runner: publishes /map + follows /planned_path)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 run robo_project runner_node
# ready when: "MAP BROADCAST SUCCESSFUL! Check RViz now."  -> map appears in RViz

terminal 6  (motion planner: A* from the robot to the goal)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
python3 install/robo_project/lib/robo_project/motion_planner
# run it with the conda python (NOT "ros2 run": that uses /usr/bin/python3, which has no numba,
# and A* then falls back to the slow pure-Python search: seconds instead of ~10 ms).
# plans to GOAL_X/GOAL_Y (0,0) at start; the robot drives it in Habitat and RViz.
# Click "2D Goal Pose" in RViz to send a new goal - it re-plans from the current pose.
# Obstacles seen by the ML model (terminal 7, /fusion/obstacle_map) are added to the A* map;
# when one lies on the current path it re-plans at once ("ML model: obstacle on the path").
# If the robot still gets stuck, runner_node reports it on /blocked_point and it re-plans too.
# No path at all: the robot is stopped and planning is retried every 2 s.

terminal 7  (fusion ML model: 4 RGB cameras + LiDAR + depth -> ML obstacle map for the planner)

conda activate habitat
cd ~/robo_project_ws
source install/setup.bash
ros2 run robo_project fusion_obstacle_node
# needs runs/fusion_full_e1.2/best.pt in the workspace (copied from still_robo_project_ws)
# ready when: "Obstacle map 768x1024 ... aligned with /map" (needs runner_node's /map)
# every prediction (~10/s, ~85 ms each on CPU) is fused into /fusion/obstacle_map (aligned with
# /map, log-odds over time) -> motion_planner avoids those obstacles.
# RViz: "ML Obstacle Map" (what the planner avoids), "Fusion Local Grid" (raw 1.2 m prediction),
# "LiDAR" (simulated scan).

notes
